# Licensing

KinRin is a **container image**, not a single work of authorship, so it cannot
carry one covering licence. It bundles components under at least three different
terms plus one with none, and `GPL-2.0-only` is not a valid umbrella: it cannot
cover Niri's `GPL-3.0-or-later`.

PLAN §10 therefore resolves to **per-component notices**, which is what this file
is. It covers the components the image is assembled from, by category, and names
each component's own authoritative licence file as the source of truth.

## The image bundles

| Component | Licence | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Fedora base and packages | **GPL-2.0-only**, plus per-package terms | `quay.io/fedora/fedora-kinoite:latest` and everything `dnf` installs from official Fedora repos. Each package's own spec governs it; `rpm -q --qf '%{LICENSE}\n' <pkg>` reports the authoritative value. |
| niri | **GPL-3.0-or-later** | <https://github.com/niri-wm/niri> |
| DankMaterialShell (`dms`, `dms-cli`) | **MIT** | <https://github.com/AvengeMedia/DankMaterialShell> |
| `dms-greeter` | as declared by its own package | Installed from the COPR's second stanza. Its repository is a **candidate** read out of the spec's `URL:` field, not a verified identity, so no licence is asserted here. |
| Dracula DMS theme | **no licence declared** | See below. |

### The one component with no licence

`/usr/share/dms-themes/dracula/theme.json` is fetched from the **DMS plugin
registry**, not from the dracula organisation:

```
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AvengeMedia/dms-plugin-registry/master/themes/dracula/theme.json
```

The source repository declares **no licence at all** for this file, and none for
the repository itself. It therefore cannot be filed under dracula's MIT, and it
carries its own line here as an **unlicensed component**. It is a JSON colour
definition, not artwork.

**Nothing else from the dracula organisation is installed.** That was verified
against the GitHub API rather than assumed:

- `dracula/kde` returns **404** — there is no GPL-3.0 KDE tree, and no
  `metadata.desktop` carrying `X-KDE-PluginInfo-License=GPLv3` exists anywhere to
  point at, so that citation is unavailable rather than merely unwanted.
- `dracula/gtk` does exist, and `dracula/dracula-theme` ships per-app trees
  (`themes/gtk`, `themes/kate`, `themes/konsole`, `themes/qt5`, …) — none of
  which this image installs.

Theming is DMS plus matugen only, which is what sidesteps the question: matugen
repaints colours and leaves widget style, icons and cursor alone, so Breeze stays
underneath and covers whatever the colour scheme does not reach.

### Proprietary components installed from RPM Fusion

`steam` and `steam-devices` (from `rpmfusion-nonfree`) and `discord` (also from
`rpmfusion-nonfree`) are **proprietary** and are redistributed under their own
terms by RPM Fusion, not under this file. They are accepted knowingly: neither
has an upstream `.src.rpm`, so RPM Fusion is the only sane non-Flathub route for
either. Their terms apply to the packages themselves; this repository's own
licence does not extend to them.

`orca` is installed from its own GitHub release RPM
(<https://github.com/stablyai/orca>) at build time, so it is neither vendored
here nor covered here.

